    "long_instructions": "## Stage Director\r\n\r\nMake an object appear in a different place each time the program runs.\r\n\r\n1. Review the code and ask AI Tutor how `draw_ellipse()` works.\r\n2. Use `randint()` to store random values for the x-position and y-position. The values can be from 0 to 400.\r\n3. Update the `draw_ellipse()` command to use your variables.\r\n4. Run the program several times and observe where the object appears.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from theater import *\nfrom random import randint\n\n# Night sky\nset_fill_color(\"black\")\ndraw_rectangle(0, 0, 400, 400)\n\n# Moon\nset_fill_color(\"ivory\")\ndraw_ellipse(280, 60, 70, 70)\n\n# Stars\nset_fill_color(\"white\")\ndraw_ellipse(40, 50, 5, 5)\ndraw_ellipse(125, 120, 4, 4)\ndraw_ellipse(290, 70, 6, 6)\ndraw_ellipse(350, 150, 5, 5)\ndraw_ellipse(80, 210, 4, 4)\ndraw_ellipse(230, 180, 5, 5)\n\n# Music notes\nset_text_color(\"aqua\")\nset_text_height(30)\ndraw_text(\"♪\", 70, 300)\ndraw_text(\"♫\", 310, 255)\ndraw_text(\"♪\", 245, 320)\n\n# Title\nset_text_color(\"ivory\")\nset_text_height(28)\ndraw_text(\"Moonrise Melody\", 95, 360)\n\n\n# Twinkle Twinkle melody\nplay_note_and_pause(72, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(72, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(79, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(79, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(81, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(81, 0.5)\nplay_note_and_pause(79, 0.8)\n\nplay()",
